## REST contract for each API base

GET base lists `{items, page, size, total}`; GET base/count counts matching rows.
GET base/item?id=... reads an item. For writable entities, POST base creates
(201), PUT base/item?id=... replaces mutable attributes (200), DELETE
base/item?id=... removes (204). Missing items return 404, malformed/invalid input
400 and declared database constraint conflicts 409. Identity is immutable.
Assigned identities must be included in the body; generated UUID identities
are omitted. JSON property names are SQL column names from the table below;
omitted nullable attributes on PUT become null. Unknown properties are rejected.
IDs use query parameters so text identifiers may contain reserved path characters.

List/count accept page (default 0, maximum 1000000), size (1..100, default 20),
sort (a declared sortable column or primary key), direction (asc/desc),
filter.COLUMN=value (typed equality, AND), and q (case-insensitive literal
substring over explicitly searchable text attributes, OR). Sort defaults to the
primary key and adds it as a tie breaker. Duplicate or unknown parameters fail.
Filter "null" is the literal text value; there is no implicit null-query operator.
At most 20 query parameters and 512 characters per value are accepted.

GET base/references/FK_NAME?id=... returns a referenced item (204 if unset).
GET base/related/FK_NAME?id=... lists incoming references with the same bounded
list query. Database foreign keys reject missing references and restricted deletes.
Reference fields are scalar IDs: no nested-object or implicit cascade writes.

